{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/594837-changeling-sailors-court-or-entitlement","id":594837,"title":"Changeling Sailors: Court or Entitlement?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-18T10:40:40-07:00","id":594837,"title":"Changeling Sailors: Court or Entitlement?","content":"I was thinking of the best way to handle pirate stories in Changeling 2E; and not just for a golden age of piracy Dark Era, with the hedge you could basically play Pirates of the Caribbean in the modern day, with 17th century hobgoblin port towns and all manner of weirdness on the hedge sea.<br /> <br /> The question I had was how do Bulwarks work when a Changling is out on a long sea voyage? Courts are geographically based so it feels like the Bulwark shouldn't protect you away from home, and even if it did how many Changelings would want to rely on a Bulwark being maintained where they can't see it? That's a lot of trust to place in a Freehold.<br /> <br /> <br /> So the obvious solution is that sailors are a special case, where every ship has it's own Bulwark and Changelings can have two Mantles. One applies when they're on a ship or on shore leave, the other applies when they're in their home Freehold.<br /> <br /> Which leads me to my question. Should I just write it up as a Court that has a weird and unexplained ability for dual memberships or should there be a &quot;ship captain&quot; Entitlement who's ability is to create a one-ship Freehold that uses the Court mechanics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T10:52:02-07:00","id":594860,"title":"","content":"It really does depend on the game. If the emphasis really is a sort of &quot;Road Culture of the Ocean&quot;, then Courts are the way to go. If it's centered on a port, then go with Entitlements.<br /> <br /> Never hurts to imagine them up as both, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T11:16:36-07:00","id":594871,"title":"","content":"You know me Arc <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> this is for a homebrew not a specific game.<br /> <br /> That said the emphasis is on a &quot;Road Culture of the Ocean&quot; which is why it's either going to be a Court (well lots of Courts, 1 per ship) or an Entitlement who's powers make it a Court in all but name.<br /> <br /> <br /> The question is really; should I use the presence of an Entitlement to justify allowing dual Court membership or should I just allow dual Court membership regardless. It comes down to whether this fits the role of 2E entitlements (which we don't know yet, but maybe MachineIV will drop by this thread) and whether neat ideas like every captain having to start off on another ship and &quot;learn the ways of the see&quot; justify the fact a captain couldn't be a member of another Entitlement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T11:27:02-07:00","id":594874,"title":"","content":"With no other specifics, I'd go Courts. it fits the idea<br /> <br /> THAT SAID, If I were doing this as a game at my table, I'd go with Entitlements for ship crews and Courts for their employers, because I would set it in the Golden Age of Piracy and look at the government supported pirates, emphasizing the disconnect between loyalties of crew versus state, as well as the emergent community of piracy, just really pull on the three links of chain there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T11:49:01-07:00","id":594889,"title":"","content":"Also, if it's for Homebrew, than I really don't see a case for a &quot;Why not both&quot;. You're not serving any needs anyways, might as well just make for all the angles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T16:43:14-07:00","id":595113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/594837-changeling-sailors-court-or-entitlement?p=594874#post594874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THAT SAID, If I were doing this as a game at my table, I'd go with Entitlements for ship crews and Courts for their employers, because I would set it in the Golden Age of Piracy and look at the government supported pirates, emphasizing the disconnect between loyalties of crew versus state, as well as the emergent community of piracy, just really pull on the three links of chain there.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works fine in both versions.<br /> <br /> Take Pirates of the Carribian. Captain Jack Sparrow belongs to the Black Perl and the Brethren Court. While James Norrington belongs to the Dauntless and the British Empire.<br /> <br /> You could play that that both Sparrow and Norrington are in the sailor Entitlement. Norrington has an oath of feilty to the monarch of the Britsh Empire. And the Brethren Court are a group within in the Sailor Entitlement.<br /> <br /> Or you could just say it's two ship-courts, two court-courts, and both people have dual membership.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/594837-changeling-sailors-court-or-entitlement?p=594889#post594889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if it's for Homebrew, than I really don't see a case for a &quot;Why not both&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Personal taste. I like to think of my homebrew as all part of a cohesive setting so I usually won't do two different representations of the same thing. Plus, it wouldn't be fun to write.<br /> <br /> (I think the Order of St. Anthony is the only time I did; but honestly - the Conspiracy version is basically a flat out replacement for the Compact)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}